    "body": "### Problem\n\n`gv` not restore visual selection for each cursor\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. nvim --clean\n2. some text:\n```text\naaa\nbbb\nccc\n```\n3. `Q` place cursor on each word, and then type `q=`\n4. type `viw`\n5. type `<Esc>`\n6. type `gv`, it only restore the visual selection for primary cursor\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`gv` should restore visual selection for each cursor.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1473+g9a29622b54\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n6.18.26.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwindows terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub download",
